The IOC Container creates separate object for Spring bean class for every ctx.getBean() method call 
and that spring class object will not be placed in the internal cache of IOC container

If the spring bean class obj state is changing time to time then it is recomended to take the scope
as the "prototype" scope so that for every data change one new obj will be created for the spring 
bean

@Lazy(true) is application only for the singleton scope spring beans to disable the pre/eager instantiation
on singleton scope spring bean 
@Lazy(true) does not give effect on other scope spring beans becoz they are always enable with lazy instantation


if the spring bean scope is "prototype" the spring  bean class obj ref will not be placed in the internal cache of the
IOC container,So ctx.getBean() does not find prototype scope spring bean
class obj ref in the internal cache of the IOC container hence it creates new object for every
ctx.getBean() method call
